  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25145558",
      "title": "Styling Components In Next.js Projects",
      "lectureOrder": 251,
      "videoOrder": 234,
      "sourceHash": "b6d52495fbe7fda2a2f8c61a5c939a216b37332e18327972d218e28a408e155b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.08,
          "end": 5.01,
          "en": "How do we style our next application?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.01,
          "end": 7.79,
          "en": "How do we style our components?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.79,
          "end": 10.28,
          "en": "Generally that is totally up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 10.28,
          "end": 13.67,
          "en": "Next JS supports styled components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.67,
          "end": 16.39,
          "en": "You can use regular HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.39,
          "end": 20.37,
          "en": "with regular selectors, classes and so on,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.37,
          "end": 24.3,
          "en": "and you can also use CSS Modules.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.3,
          "end": 26.85,
          "en": "And the support for the latter is actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.85,
          "end": 30.58,
          "en": "already built into a next JS project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.58,
          "end": 32.63,
          "en": "Now that is what I'm going to use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.63,
          "end": 35.77,
          "en": "so that we have scoped CSS styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.77,
          "end": 39.87,
          "en": "scoped to specific components, at least if we want to.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 39.87,
          "end": 43.03,
          "en": "But you can definitely also explore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.03,
          "end": 46.46,
          "en": "other approaches for styling components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.46,
          "end": 49.79,
          "en": "Now you will notice that we have this styles folder here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 49.79,
          "end": 52.92,
          "en": "and in there we have a global CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.92,
          "end": 56.55,
          "en": "Now here I set up some global CSS styles for you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 58.03,
          "en": "and as I just said,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.03,
          "end": 63.03,
          "en": "you could, of course, add more classes here and then simply,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.07,
          "end": 65.74,
          "en": "well, set up any styles you want here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.74,
          "end": 68.6,
          "en": "And you can also add more CSS files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 68.6,
          "end": 72.91,
          "en": "and for example, import them in this app JS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 72.91,
          "end": 77.66,
          "en": "where we are also already importing globals CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.66,
          "end": 78.98,
          "en": "And we haven't really learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 78.98,
          "end": 81.62,
          "en": "what the role of this app JS file is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 81.62,
          "end": 84.25,
          "en": "But for the moment, you can keep in mind that here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 84.25,
          "end": 89.25,
          "en": "you could definitely import all your global CSS files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 90.2,
          "end": 93.41,
          "en": "But I want to be able to scope styles to components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 93.41,
          "end": 97.97999999999999,
          "en": "and therefore I will use the built in CSS Module support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 97.97999999999999,
          "end": 99.22,
          "en": "Now, in case you don't know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 99.22,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "CSS Modules is all about setting up CSS code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 106.15,
          "en": "which is then bound to a single component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 106.15,
          "end": 109.25,
          "en": "so it does only affect that component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 109.25,
          "end": 111.58,
          "en": "and no other component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 111.58,
          "end": 113.31,
          "en": "And that's a nice little feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 113.31,
          "end": 115.25999999999999,
          "en": "which ensures that our styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 115.25999999999999,
          "end": 118.8,
          "en": "don't spill over to other components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.8,
          "end": 122.01,
          "en": "Now, therefore, I will create a separate CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.01,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "for the event-item component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "A CSS file where I will define the styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 128.52,
          "en": "for that component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.52,
          "end": 132.53,
          "en": "And I could create that CSS file in the styles folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 132.53,
          "end": 135.9,
          "en": "and import it from there and that would work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.9,
          "end": 139.63,
          "en": "But I will create the next to the event-item.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.63,
          "end": 143.75,
          "en": "so that component code and component styles,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.75,
          "end": 146.1,
          "en": "are located in the same place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.1,
          "end": 149.16,
          "en": "That is a convention I like to follow.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.16,
          "end": 153.88,
          "en": "It makes it easier to find the styles for a given component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.88,
          "end": 157.13,
          "en": "Therefore, here we add a new CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 157.13,
          "end": 159.01,
          "en": "we could name it event-item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.01,
          "end": 163.99,
          "en": "But to unlock this CSS Module feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 163.99,
          "end": 168.55700000000002,
          "en": "this file actually has to end with .module.css.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 169.9,
          "end": 173.167,
          "en": "So event - item .module.CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.36,
          "end": 176.8,
          "en": "The part here event - item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.8,
          "end": 179.65,
          "en": "that's up to you, that does not matter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.65,
          "end": 184.65,
          "en": "But the ending .module.CSS, that is important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 184.91,
          "end": 186.88,
          "en": "Now with that we can save this file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 186.88,
          "end": 191.59,
          "en": "and now in event-item.JS we can import this file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 191.59,
          "end": 195.45,
          "en": "We can import a CSS file into a JavaScript file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 195.45,
          "end": 196.9,
          "en": "and behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 196.9,
          "end": 200.96,
          "en": "the next JS build process will take care about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 200.96,
          "end": 204.04,
          "en": "It will basically extract the CSS code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 204.04,
          "end": 205.9,
          "en": "change to selectors a little bit",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 205.9,
          "end": 210.26,
          "en": "to scope them to this component HTML code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 210.26,
          "end": 213.04,
          "en": "and inject it into the running page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 213.04,
          "end": 215.27,
          "en": "We don't need to worry about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 215.27,
          "end": 218.09,
          "en": "we just need to import our CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 218.09,
          "end": 221.73,
          "en": "Our event - item .module.CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 221.73,
          "end": 223.7,
          "en": "However, not just like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 223.7,
          "end": 226.75,
          "en": "instead we import classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 226.75,
          "end": 230.22,
          "en": "or styles the name is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.22,
          "end": 235.22,
          "en": "I'll go with classes from event-item .module.CSS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 235.75,
          "end": 237.99,
          "en": "This is required for using",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 237.99,
          "end": 240.93,
          "en": "this CSS Modules feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 240.93,
          "end": 245.04,
          "en": "This classes thing here will be an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.04,
          "end": 247.5,
          "en": "where all the CSS classes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 247.5,
          "end": 250.29,
          "en": "we define in this CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 250.29,
          "end": 253.87,
          "en": "will be exposed under their class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 253.87,
          "end": 257.84,
          "en": "so that we can assign them to HTML elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 257.84,
          "end": 261.16,
          "en": "This is required because the CSS class names",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.16,
          "end": 264.01,
          "en": "we will add in this CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.01,
          "end": 267.79,
          "en": "will be transformed under the port by the build process",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 267.79,
          "end": 270.32,
          "en": "to make them unique for this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 270.32,
          "end": 272.3,
          "en": "I also do talk about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 272.3,
          "end": 274.77,
          "en": "in my \"React- The Complete Guide\" course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 274.77,
          "end": 277.18,
          "en": "in case you wanna dive a bit deeper.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 277.18,
          "end": 281,
          "en": "Therefore, we import classes from this CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 281,
          "end": 286,
          "en": "and then we can, for example, go to our list item here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 286.12,
          "end": 289.03499999999997,
          "en": "add the className property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 289.03499999999997,
          "end": 291.56,
          "en": "the className attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 291.56,
          "end": 295.32,
          "en": "and set this equal not to a string,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 295.32,
          "end": 297.693,
          "en": "but instead to a dynamic value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.65999999999997,
          "end": 302.45,
          "en": "specifically to some key we get from this classes object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 302.45,
          "end": 304.443,
          "en": "And here that should be the item key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 305.59,
          "end": 307.64,
          "en": "Now, in these CSS file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.64,
          "end": 310.11,
          "en": "we can add a item class selector,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 310.11,
          "end": 312.9,
          "en": "so that name here has to match",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 312.9,
          "end": 315.45,
          "en": "that name which we're accessing here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 315.45,
          "end": 318.02,
          "en": "And now we can to find the styles in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318.02,
          "end": 321.64,
          "en": "which will be applied to only this list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 321.64,
          "end": 326.22,
          "en": "So even if we would use the item class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 326.22,
          "end": 329.493,
          "en": "let's say in the event list component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 330.335,
          "end": 333.82,
          "en": "if I would add this kind of className here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 333.82,
          "end": 336.79,
          "en": "even then these style set up here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 336.79,
          "end": 341.45,
          "en": "would not affect this one here, this unordered list item.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 341.45,
          "end": 343.887,
          "en": "Because with the CSS Marshalls feature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 343.887,
          "end": 347.65,
          "en": "the className we assign here in the CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 347.65,
          "end": 350.73,
          "en": "will be changed under.behind the scenes,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 350.73,
          "end": 352.65,
          "en": "and it will no longer be item",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 352.65,
          "end": 355.64,
          "en": "once the application runs in the browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 355.64,
          "end": 359.35,
          "en": "Therefore, to get this magically changed filename,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 359.35,
          "end": 362.6,
          "en": "we get access to those transformed classNames",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 362.6,
          "end": 365.45,
          "en": "under this important classes object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 365.45,
          "end": 369.33,
          "en": "and we then access our originally assigned className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 369.33,
          "end": 372.24,
          "en": "and get access to the actual transformed className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 372.24,
          "end": 375.69,
          "en": "and assign this as a className to the list item then.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 375.69,
          "end": 377,
          "en": "It sounds confusing?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 377,
          "end": 378.56,
          "en": "Let me show it to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 378.56,
          "end": 382.34,
          "en": "If we temporarily give this a color of red,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 382.34,
          "end": 384.37,
          "en": "so if that's the style we assign,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 384.37,
          "end": 387.18,
          "en": "and we then save all the files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 387.18,
          "end": 391.15,
          "en": "if I now reload and I then inspect this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 391.15,
          "end": 393.808,
          "en": "you will see that this list item,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 393.808,
          "end": 395.90999999999997,
          "en": "has a class of event - item underscore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 397.052,
          "end": 400.37,
          "en": "item underscore underscore some unique hash.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 400.37,
          "end": 404.89,
          "en": "And that's not the className we defined in the CSS file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 404.89,
          "end": 408.3,
          "en": "Instead, that is this transformed className",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 408.3,
          "end": 411.63,
          "en": "and the link is made through our assignment",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 412.618,
          "end": 414.003,
          "en": "of classes.item here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 415.02,
          "end": 416.77,
          "en": "So that's not working under dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 416.77,
          "end": 420.11,
          "en": "and it allows us to scope our CSS styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 420.11,
          "end": 422.07,
          "en": "to a selected component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 422.07,
          "end": 426.72,
          "en": "Now, with that attached you find two CSS files,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 426.72,
          "end": 428.69,
          "en": "which I prepared for you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
